Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 20:54:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix broken build: create missing logs modules, fix bad import
 path

The dev-branch build was broken - verified with 'npm run build',
which failed outright ('Could not resolve ../logs/test_aiagent.js
from src/App.jsx').

Root cause: the default Vite .gitignore has a blanket 'logs' rule
meant for log-output folders, but this repo repurposes logs/ as a
real source directory. That silently kept src/logs/test_aiagent.js
and src/logs/reflectionLog.js out of version control, so App.jsx
and KPITracker.jsx were importing files that existed locally for
whoever wrote them but never actually got committed.

- Added !src/logs/ to .gitignore so this can't happen again
- Added src/logs/test_aiagent.js (numerology6_directives, plus a
  numerology7_directives scaffold per the README TODO - not yet
  wired into App.jsx)
- Added src/logs/reflectionLog.js (phaseClock, taskChecklist)
- Fixed App.jsx's test_aiagent.js import, which used '../logs/'
  (repo root) while the sibling reflectionLog.js import two lines
  below it correctly used './logs/' (src/logs) - inconsistent
  depth was a second, separate bug. KPITracker.jsx already had
  the correct relative path.
- Removed leftover chat text pasted into the bottom of README.md,
  checked off the completed TODO item

Verified: npm run build now succeeds.
